  "body": "## What changed\n\nRotary Contour generates rings around a cylindrical workpiece along X.\nFor a nearly horizontal axis, top and bottom specify axial ball-center stations.\nClearance and retract specify tool-tip radii about the fitted axis.\nThe planner reuses waterline contact geometry and radial links.\nIt refuses unsafe radii and invalid station bounds by name.\nThe decision record explains the parameter contract and alternatives.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe station conversion divided world height by the fitted axis Z component.\nAn X axis has a zero Z component, so the generator refused it.\nRemoving that refusal alone would retain the invalid division and axial links.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe initial geometry pin failed on unchanged upstream/main `97a880c53`.\nThe motion pins measure complete rings, axial bounds, radial poses, and link clearance:\n\n- `rotary_contour_x_generates_complete_radial_rings`\n- `rotary_contour_x_uses_the_translated_axis_for_clearance`\n- `rotary_contour_x_refuses_clearance_inside_the_work_by_name`\n- `rotary_contour_x_refuses_retract_inside_the_work_by_name`\n- `rotary_contour_x_refuses_an_invalid_station_window_by_name`\n\nAll five pins failed with the original generator restored from upstream/main.\nAll five passed after the fixed generator was restored.\nThis mutation includes each new input guard.\n\nThe app pins passed on the real Tormach microARC machine definition:\n\n- `rotary_contour_x_verifies_and_posts_finite_a_moves`\n- `rotary_contour_x_in_oversized_stock_still_blocks_posting`\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 10 steps.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nI did not run the GUI, a physical machine, or the batch, release, and heavy gates.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR touched the expected files during the overlap check.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Rotary Contour generates verified rings for cylindrical workpieces on A about X.\n\nFixes #3000\n",
